# Curved app bar

Standard screens use [`CurvedAppBar`](lib/core/ui/widgets/curved_app_bar.dart) inside
[`CurvedAppBarLayout`](lib/core/ui/widgets/curved_app_bar.dart) — **not** on
`Scaffold.appBar` and not raw `AppBar(...)`.

The bar is painted in a `Stack` so body content starts **below** the curved
bottom edge and the curve stays visible.

## When to use

- Home, settings, lists, forms, and any pushed route that needs a title bar
- Drawer screens: `CurvedAppBar(..., showDrawerMenu: true)` inside the layout
- Pushed screens: default back button (`automaticallyImplyLeading: true`)

## When NOT to use

- First-start onboarding (language / theme) with inline back button and no top bar
- Full-screen dialogs, splash, or screens that deliberately hide the bar

## Usage

```dart
import '../widgets/curved_app_bar.dart';

Scaffold(
  drawer: myDrawer, // optional
  body: CurvedAppBarLayout(
    appBar: CurvedAppBar(
      title: S.current.homePage,
      showDrawerMenu: true,
      automaticallyImplyLeading: false,
    ),
    body: _HomeBody(),
  ),
)
```

Full-screen background + bar overlay:

```dart
Scaffold(
  body: Stack(
    fit: StackFit.expand,
    children: [
      const MyBackground(),
      CurvedAppBarLayout(
        appBar: CurvedAppBar(title: S.current.someTitle),
        body: _ScreenContent(),
      ),
    ],
  ),
)
```

Optional: `titleWidget`, `leading`, `actions`, `centerTitle`, `bottomCurveRadius`,
`bodyTopGap` on `CurvedAppBarLayout` (default `12` logical gap below the curve).

## Spacing

- Use `CurvedAppBar.bodyTopPadding(context)` only when building a custom stack;
  prefer `CurvedAppBarLayout` so inset stays consistent.
- Do not add manual `SafeArea` top padding on the body — the layout already
  accounts for status bar + toolbar + curve.

## Styling rules

- Colors come from `Theme.of(context).colorScheme` inside the widget
- Title uses `textTheme.titleLarge` with `onPrimary`
- Status bar overlay is handled by the bar; do not duplicate `AnnotatedRegion`
  on the same screen unless the body extends behind the bar intentionally

## Do / don't

```dart
// ❌ BAD — separates bar from body; curve gets clipped
appBar: CurvedAppBar(title: S.current.homePage),

// ❌ BAD
appBar: AppBar(title: Text(S.current.homePage)),

// ✅ GOOD
body: CurvedAppBarLayout(
  appBar: CurvedAppBar(title: S.current.homePage, showDrawerMenu: true),
  body: ...,
),
```

When adding a new screen, default to `CurvedAppBarLayout` unless the design
matches the onboarding (no bar) pattern.
